drome HPO terms associated with each disease were also pulled from the HPO files for mapping. The Alzheimer and COVID sets were created by identifying symptoms and signs for patients from the literature then identifying the relevant MP and HP terms and finally mapping the identified terms to terms in the other ontology. Use of skos mappings terms: exact match: MP term is the same as the HPO term, ignoring that the HP term applies only to humans; broad match: HPO term covers more than the MP term, ignoring the species restriction; narrow match: HPO term is more restricted than the MP term; related match: MP term and HPO term share some similarity but would not have a parent-child relation in a shared ontology.\",\"mapping_set_id\":\"https://w3id.org/sssom/commons/mouse-human/mappings/mp_hp_mgi_all.sssom.tsv\",\"mapping_set_title\":\"All mappings of MP terms to HPO terms generated by MGI\"},\"fields\":{\"author_id\":[\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597\"],\"comment\":\"KidsFirst; existing annotations from J:15425, J:98554 annotations are scattered under various terms, https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/3511\",\"confidence\":1,\"mapping_date\":\"2022-02-07\",\"mapping_justification\":\"https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/ManualMappingCuration\",\"object_id\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000033\",\"object_label\":\"Ambiguous genitalia male\",\"object_source\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/hp\",\"predicate_id\":\"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrowMatch\",\"subject_id\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0009198\",\"subject_label\":\"abnormal male genitalia morphology\",\"subject_source\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mp\"}}","exitCode":0,"signal":null,"stdout":"\"sha256:86fa00b141f0c2c0a96f7c083e01f6ad57772634e9a6e58c037f3d72d226cd50\"\n","stderr":"","processError":null},{"command":["/var/folders/tr/qmsqldfn59591rbflj14mc4r0000gn/T/patamaps-discovery-api-_9iocgp5/patamaps","json","digest"],"input":"{\"content\":\"sha256:86f